comment:  F-PC native port.

  SFLOAT is still a software floating point package with its own float
  stack and its own number format, so that its high level words (which
  poke at exponents with  n FSP @ +!  and compare FPSEXP values) work
  unchanged.  The representation is the original 48-bit one, kept in
  memory exactly as before:

        +0  16 bits  sign ($8000) and exponent (15 bits, bias $3FFF)
        +2  16 bits  high half of the 32-bit significand
        +4  16 bits  low half of the significand

  The significand has its binary point before the leading bit, which is
  always set; a number whose leading bit is clear counts as zero.
  F#BYTES is still 6, and the halves are read and written with W@ W!.

  On the parameter stack (FPOP FPUSH FPCOPY FPFRACT FPSEXP) the three
  16-bit fields are three cells, as before: ( lo hi sx ).  lo and hi are
  0..$FFFF; sx (and FPSEXP) is sign-extended, so  FPSEXP 0<  still tests
  the sign.  FPUSH keeps the low 16 bits of each cell, so all the hex
  constants (DAA2 C90F 4001 FPUSH ...) are unchanged.

  The 8086 CODE words were rewritten in high level Forth:
  - F+ F- F* F/ FSQRT FLOAT TFLOAT round to nearest even, as the CODE
    did, but work on the 32-bit significand in one cell (UM* UM/MOD and
    64-bit doubles replace the 16-bit carry chains).  The results should
    be the same bit for bit.
  - The polynomial and table kernels (FLN, GEXP1, AUXTAN, AUXATAN) are
    computed with the VM's native double precision floats and rounded to
    the 48-bit format.  They are at least as accurate as before.
  - Doubles are 64 bits: FLOAT takes, and FIX INT give, 64-bit doubles;
    triple numbers (TINTA, UMT*, TFLOAT) are three 32-bit cells.
  Do not load SFLOAT and FFLOAT together: both define F+ F@ F. etc.
comment;

DEFINED NOFLOATING NIP #IF NOFLOATING #THEN

ANEW FPPACKAGE
\ PREFIX                \ F-PC native port: no 8086 assembler
\ LOADED,
DECIMAL
6 CONSTANT F#BYTES              \ Number of bytes for a floating point number
CREATE FPSTAT 0 , 0 ,           \ Holds error information

ALSO HIDDEN DEFINITIONS
40 F#BYTES * CONSTANT FPSSIZE   \ Size of floating point stack
CREATE FPSTACK   FPSSIZE ALLOT  \ Floating Point Stack is separate
PREVIOUS DEFINITIONS

HERE 12 ALLOT                   \ Leave a little room for underflow
CONSTANT FSP0                   \ Point to base of stack.
CREATE FSP   FSP0 ,             \ Points to top of stack
                                \ F-PC native port: this hides the VM's FSP

HEX

: FDEPTHB   ( -- n )             \ Depth of floating point stack in bytes.
        FSP0 FSP @ - ;

: FDEPTH   ( -- n )             \ Depth of floating point stack in FP words.
        FDEPTHB 6 / ;

: FCLEAR   ( -- )                 \ Clear Floating Point Stack.
        FSP0 FSP ! ;

: AND!   ( n addr -- )       \ Logical AND of contents at addr with n
        TUCK @ AND SWAP ! ;  \ F-PC native port: was CODE

: OR!   ( n addr -- )        \ Logical OR of contents at addr with n
        TUCK @ OR SWAP ! ;   \ F-PC native port: was CODE

: SX>N   ( u16 -- n )        \ F-PC native port: sign-extend 16 bits
        $8000 XOR $8000 - ;

: W+!   ( n addr -- )        \ F-PC native port: 16-bit +!, for the idiom
        TUCK W@ + SWAP W! ;  \ n FSP @ W+! (add n to the top exponent)

: FPOP   ( F: r -- ; -- d n )   \ Pop floating number from f-stack to
        FSP @ DUP 4 + W@        \ parameter stack.
        OVER 2+ W@ ROT W@ SX>N
        6 FSP +! ;

: FPUSH   ( F: -- r ; d n -- )    \ Push floating number from parameter
        -6 FSP +! FSP @           \ stack to floating stack.
        TUCK W! TUCK 2+ W! 4 + W! ;

: FPCOPY  ( F r -- r ; -- d n )      \ Get a copy of the floating number
        FSP @ DUP 4 + W@             \ at top of floating stack.
        OVER 2+ W@ ROT W@ SX>N ;

: FPFRACT  ( F: r -- r ; -- d )
        FSP @ DUP 4 + W@ SWAP 2+ W@ ;

: FPSEXP  ( F: r -- r ; -- n )
        FSP @ W@ SX>N ;

: 2/?   ( n1 -- n2 n3 )         \ n2 is n1 shifted right by 1.
                                \ n3 is least significant bit of n1 .
        DUP >R 2/ 7FFF AND R> 1 AND ;

: .NAME     ( n1 -- )
        >NAME .ID ;

DEFER FPERR

ALSO HIDDEN DEFINITIONS

: .FP.    ( -- )   ." Floating Point " ;

: (FPERR)    ( F: r -- r ; n1 n2 --  )       \ n1 is CFA, n2 is error flag.
        DUP FPSTAT OR!  CR  BELL EMIT
 ( 1 )  2/? IF  DROP .FP. ." Division by zero in "          .NAME EXIT THEN
 ( 2 )  2/? IF  DROP .FP. ." Overflow in "                  .NAME EXIT THEN
 ( 4 )  2/? IF  DROP .FP. ." argument is negative for "     .NAME EXIT THEN
 ( 8 )  2/? IF  DROP .FP. ." argument is zero for "         .NAME EXIT THEN
( 10 )  2/? IF  DROP .FP. ." argument is out of range for " .NAME EXIT THEN
( 20 )  2/? IF  DROP .FP. ." Overflow for Input in "        .NAME EXIT THEN
( 40 )  2/? IF  DROP .FP. ." Overflow for Output in "       .NAME EXIT THEN
( 80 )  2/? IF  DROP ." Integer overflow for "              .NAME EXIT THEN
( 100)  2/? IF  DROP .FP. ." Underflow in "                 .NAME EXIT THEN
( 200)  2/? IF  DROP .FP. ." argument inaccurate for "      .NAME EXIT THEN
( 400)  2/? IF  DROP .FP. ." Underflow for Input in "       .NAME EXIT THEN
( 800)  2/? IF  DROP .FP. ." Underflow for Ouput in "       .NAME EXIT THEN
( 1000) 2/? IF  DROP .FP. ." results inaccurate for "       .NAME EXIT THEN
        IF ." Unspecified Error " THEN
        DROP QUIT ;

' (FPERR) IS FPERR

\ ---------------------------------------------------------------------
\ F-PC native port: helpers that replace the DENORM label and the
\ register juggling of the CODE words.  A number is unpacked to
\ ( m sx ): m is the 32-bit significand in one cell.

: (SF@)   ( a -- m sx )
        DUP 2+ W@ 10 LSHIFT OVER 4 + W@ OR SWAP W@ ;

: (SF!)   ( m sx a -- )
        TUCK W! OVER OVER 4 + W! SWAP 10 RSHIFT SWAP 2+ W! ;

: (SFPOP)   ( F: r -- ; -- m sx )
        FSP @ (SF@) 6 FSP +! ;

: (SFPUSH)   ( F: -- r ; m sx -- )
        -6 FSP +! FSP @ (SF!) ;

VARIABLE FPOP-CFA               \ the word to name in error messages

VARIABLE M1   VARIABLE E1   VARIABLE S1         \ operand r1 (second)
VARIABLE M2   VARIABLE E2   VARIABLE S2         \ operand r2 (top)

: (OPS2)   ( F: r1 r2 -- )      \ unpack both operands
        (SFPOP) DUP 7FFF AND E2 ! 8000 AND S2 ! M2 !
        (SFPOP) DUP 7FFF AND E1 ! 8000 AND S1 ! M1 ! ;

: (OVERFLOW)   ( s n -- )      \ push the largest number, report error n
        >R -1 SWAP 7FFF OR (SFPUSH) FPOP-CFA @ R> FPERR ;

\ Round the 64-bit significand ( lo hi ) to 32 bits (to nearest, ties to
\ even), then push it with exponent e and sign s.  hi must be normalized
\ (top bit set) or the result is zero.  Underflow gives zero; overflow
\ gives the largest number and an error, as the CODE words did.
: (RPACK)   ( lo hi e s -- ) ( F: -- r )
        >R >R
        DUP 0< 0= IF  2DROP R> R> 2DROP 0 0 (SFPUSH) EXIT  THEN
        SWAP DUP 80000000 U> SWAP 80000000 = 2 PICK 1 AND AND OR
        IF  1+  THEN                            ( hi' )
        R> OVER 0= IF  1+ NIP 80000000 SWAP  THEN       ( m e )
        R> OVER 1 < IF  2DROP DROP 0 0 (SFPUSH) EXIT  THEN
        OVER 7FFF < 0= IF  NIP NIP 2 (OVERFLOW) EXIT  THEN
        OR (SFPUSH) ;

VARIABLE DRS-N

: (DRS)   ( lo hi n -- lo' hi' )   \ logical right shift, with a sticky bit
        DUP 0= IF  DROP EXIT  THEN
        DUP 3F > IF  DROP OR 0<> 1 AND 0 EXIT  THEN
        DUP 1F >
        IF      20 - DRS-N !  SWAP 0<> 1 AND SWAP       ( st hi )
                DRS-N @
                IF      DUP 20 DRS-N @ - LSHIFT 0<> 1 AND ROT OR SWAP
                        DRS-N @ RSHIFT
                THEN    OR 0 EXIT
        THEN
        DRS-N !
        OVER 20 DRS-N @ - LSHIFT 0<> 1 AND >R
        DUP 20 DRS-N @ - LSHIFT ROT DRS-N @ RSHIFT OR
        R> OR SWAP DRS-N @ RSHIFT ;

: (NORM64)   ( lo hi e -- lo' hi' e' )  \ shift left until the top bit is set
        >R
        DUP 0= IF  SWAP R> 20 - >R  THEN
        BEGIN   DUP 0< 0=  OVER 0<> 2 PICK 0<> OR AND
        WHILE   D2* R> 1- >R
        REPEAT  R> ;

PREVIOUS DEFINITIONS

\ ---------------------------------------------------------------------
\ F-PC native port: conversion to and from the VM's native doubles, for
\ the transcendental kernels in SFLOAT2 and SFLOAT3.  These are compiled
\ here, before SFLOAT redefines F+ F* FDUP ..., so that they use the
\ native words.

ALSO HIDDEN DEFINITIONS

CREATE NF-WORK 8 ALLOT

: SF>NF   ( F: r -- ) ( native F: -- x )    \ SFLOAT stack to native
        (SFPOP) OVER 0< 0= IF  2DROP 0 S>F EXIT  THEN
        DUP 7FFF AND 3FFF - 20 - >R  8000 AND >R
        0 D>F  2 S>F R> R> SWAP >R S>F F** F*
        R> IF  FNEGATE  THEN ;

: NF>SF   ( native F: x -- ) ( F: -- r )    \ native to SFLOAT stack
        NF-WORK F!  NF-WORK CELL+ @ DUP 0< 8000 AND >R  ( hi )
        DUP 14 RSHIFT 7FF AND                   ( hi ef )
        DUP 0= IF  2DROP R> DROP 0 0 (SFPUSH) EXIT  THEN        \ 0, tiny
        SWAP FFFFF AND 0B LSHIFT 80000000 OR
        NF-WORK @ 15 RSHIFT OR                  ( ef hi32 )
        NF-WORK @ 0B LSHIFT SWAP                ( ef lo32 hi32 )
        ROT 3FE - 3FFF + R> (RPACK) ;

\ expm1 by Kahan's formula: accurate near 0, where exp(x)-1 cancels.
: NFEXPM1   ( native F: x -- e^x-1 )
        FDUP FEXP FDUP 1 S>F F=
        IF      FDROP EXIT  THEN
        FDUP 1 S>F F- FDUP -1 S>F F=
        IF      FSWAP FDROP FSWAP FDROP EXIT  THEN
        FROT F* FSWAP FLN F/ ;

: NF-GEXP1   ( F: x -- [e^x-1]/x )      \ for GEXP1
        SF>NF FDUP F0=
        IF      FDROP 1 S>F                     \ GEXP1(0) = 1
        ELSE    FDUP NFEXPM1 FSWAP F/
        THEN    NF>SF ;

: NF-LN   ( m e -- ) ( F: -- ln )       \ ln(m/2^32 * 2^(e-3FFF)), m normal
        3FFF - S>F 2 S>F FLN F*  0 D>F 2 S>F 20 S>F F** F/ FLN F+
        NF>SF ;

: NF-AUXTAN   ( F: x -- tan[x]-x )
        SF>NF FDUP FTAN FSWAP F- NF>SF ;

: NF-AUXATAN   ( F: x -- x-arctan[x] )
        SF>NF FDUP FATAN F- NF>SF ;

PREVIOUS DEFINITIONS

\ ---------------------------------------------------------------------

\ F+ and F-

HEX

ALSO HIDDEN ALSO          \ F-PC native port: ":" replaces the top

\ F-PC native port: F+ was CODE (with the DENORM label).  The larger
\ operand A and the smaller B are kept as 64-bit significands, B shifted
\ right to line up with a sticky bit, so the sum rounds correctly.

: F+     ( F: r1 r2 -- r3 )
        [ LAST @ NAME> ] LITERAL FPOP-CFA !
        (OPS2)
        M2 @ 0< 0= IF  M1 @ E1 @ S1 @ OR (SFPUSH) EXIT  THEN   \ r2 = 0
        M1 @ 0< 0= IF  M2 @ E2 @ S2 @ OR (SFPUSH) EXIT  THEN   \ r1 = 0
        E1 @ E2 @ < E1 @ E2 @ = M1 @ M2 @ U< AND OR
        IF                                      \ make r1 the larger
                M1 @ M2 @ M1 ! M2 !  E1 @ E2 @ E1 ! E2 !  S1 @ S2 @ S1 ! S2 !
        THEN
        0 M2 @ E1 @ E2 @ - (DRS)                ( B )
        S1 @ S2 @ =
        IF      0 M1 @ D+                       \ add magnitudes
                DUP M1 @ U<                     \ carry out?
                IF      1 (DRS) 80000000 OR E1 @ 1+
                ELSE    E1 @
                THEN
        ELSE    0 M1 @ 2SWAP D-                 \ subtract magnitudes
                2DUP D0= IF  2DROP 0 0 (SFPUSH) EXIT  THEN
                E1 @ (NORM64)
        THEN    S1 @ (RPACK) ;

PREVIOUS PREVIOUS

: F-     ( F: r1 r2 -- r3 )
        FSP @ DUP W@ 8000 XOR SWAP W!   \ For subtraction, reverse sign and add.
        F+ ;

: F\-   ( F: r1 r2 -- r3 )     \ Reverse subtraction
        FSP @ 6 + DUP W@ 8000 XOR SWAP W!
        F+ ;

\ Floating Point Multiply.

HEX

ALSO HIDDEN ALSO          \ F-PC native port: ":" replaces the top

: F*   ( F: r1 r2 -- r3 )      \ F-PC native port: was CODE
        [ LAST @ NAME> ] LITERAL FPOP-CFA !
        (OPS2)
        M1 @ 0< M2 @ 0< AND 0=
        IF      0 0 (SFPUSH) EXIT       \ If not normal, treat as zero.
        THEN
        M1 @ M2 @ UM*  E1 @ E2 @ + 3FFF -       ( lo hi e )
        OVER 0< 0= IF  >R D2* R> 1-  THEN       \ Re-normalize.
        S1 @ S2 @ XOR (RPACK) ;

\ Floating Point Divide.

: F/    ( F: r1 r2 -- r3 )     \ F-PC native port: was CODE
        [ LAST @ NAME> ] LITERAL FPOP-CFA !
        (OPS2)
        M2 @ 0< 0=                              \ Divide by zero
        IF      S1 @ S2 @ XOR 1 (OVERFLOW) EXIT
        THEN
        M1 @ 0< 0= IF  0 0 (SFPUSH) EXIT  THEN  \ zero numerator
        E1 @ E2 @ - 3FFF +
        M1 @ M2 @ U<
        IF      0 M1 @                          \ num < den
        ELSE    1+ M1 @ 1F LSHIFT M1 @ 1 RSHIFT \ num >= den: shift right
        THEN
        M2 @ UM/MOD                             ( e rem q )
        SWAP 0 SWAP M2 @ UM/MOD                 ( e q rem2 q2 )
        SWAP IF  1 OR  THEN                     \ sticky bit
        SWAP ROT S1 @ S2 @ XOR (RPACK) ;

PREVIOUS PREVIOUS

\  End of basic 4-functions.

\  Floating Square Root

DECIMAL

ALSO HIDDEN DEFINITIONS

2VARIABLE SQ-N   2VARIABLE SQ-R   2VARIABLE SQ-B

: (ISQRT)   ( ud -- root ud-rem )       \ integer square root of 64 bits
        SQ-N 2!  0. SQ-R 2!  0 $40000000 SQ-B 2!
        32 0
        DO      SQ-R 2@ SQ-B 2@ D+              ( r+b )
                SQ-N 2@ 2OVER DU<
                IF      2DROP SQ-R 2@ D2/
                ELSE    SQ-N 2@ 2SWAP D- SQ-N 2!
                        SQ-R 2@ D2/ SQ-B 2@ D+
                THEN    SQ-R 2!
                SQ-B 2@ D2/ D2/ SQ-B 2!
        LOOP
        SQ-R 2@ DROP SQ-N 2@ ;

PREVIOUS DEFINITIONS

ALSO HIDDEN ALSO          \ F-PC native port: ":" replaces the top

: FSQRT    ( F: r1 -- r2 )      \ F-PC native port: was CODE
        (SFPOP) OVER 0< 0=
        IF      2DROP 0 0 (SFPUSH) EXIT  THEN   \ If MS bit not set, zero.
        DUP 0<  OVER $8000 AND OR
        IF      2DROP 0 -1 (SFPUSH)             \ Negative argument
                [ LAST @ NAME> ] LITERAL 4 FPERR EXIT
        THEN
        $3FFF - DUP 1 AND
        IF      1+ 2/ SWAP DUP 31 LSHIFT SWAP 1 RSHIFT  \ odd exponent
        ELSE    2/ SWAP 0 SWAP
        THEN    ROT >R                          \ N ; e' on the return stack
        (ISQRT) 2>R DUP 0 2R> DU<               ( q q<rem? )
        IF      $80000001  ELSE  0  THEN        \ rounding bits
        SWAP R> $3FFF + 0 (RPACK) ;

PREVIOUS PREVIOUS

\ End of Square-root code.

HEX

\ F-PC native port: the stack words were CODE; they move the 6-byte
\ numbers with CMOVE.

ALSO HIDDEN DEFINITIONS
CREATE FTMP 6 ALLOT

: (FADDR)   ( n -- addr )       \ address of item n of the float stack
        6 * FSP @ + ;

: (XCHG)   ( n1 n2 -- )         \ exchange items n1 and n2
        (FADDR) SWAP (FADDR)
        OVER FTMP 6 CMOVE  TUCK SWAP 6 CMOVE  FTMP SWAP 6 CMOVE ;
PREVIOUS DEFINITIONS

ALSO HIDDEN ALSO          \ F-PC native port: ":" replaces the top

: FDUP   ( F: r -- r r )
        FSP @ DUP 6 - 6 CMOVE  -6 FSP +! ;

: FDROP   ( F: r1 -- )
        6 FSP +! ;

: F2DROP   ( F: r1 r2 -- )
        0C FSP +! ;

: FNIP   ( F: r1 r2 -- r2 )
        FSP @ DUP 6 + 6 CMOVE  6 FSP +! ;

: FOVER   ( F: r1 r2 -- r1 r2 r1 )
        FSP @ DUP 6 + SWAP 6 - 6 CMOVE  -6 FSP +! ;

: F2DUP   ( F: r1 r2 -- r1 r2 r1 r2 )
        FOVER FOVER ;

: FSWAP   ( F: r1 r2 -- r2 r1 )
        0 1 (XCHG) ;

: FROT   ( F: r1 r2 r3 -- r2 r3 r1 )
        0 2 (XCHG)  1 2 (XCHG) ;

: F-ROT   ( F: r1 r2 r3 -- r3 r1 r2 )
        0 2 (XCHG)  0 1 (XCHG) ;

: FPICK  ( F: rn rn-1 ... r0 -- rn rn-1 ... r0 rn ; n -- )
        (FADDR) FSP @ 6 - 6 CMOVE  -6 FSP +! ;

: FNSWAP   ( F: rn rn-1 ... r0 -- r0 rn-1 ... r1 rn ; n -- )
        0 (XCHG) ;

\ F-PC native port: the tests were CODE.  A number is zero when the top
\ bit of its significand is clear.

: FDUP0<   ( F: r1 -- r1 ; -- flag )
        FSP @ (SF@) 8000 AND 0<> SWAP 0< AND ;

: F0<   ( F: r -- ; -- flag )
        FDUP0< FDROP ;

: F0>   ( F: r -- ; -- flag )
        FSP @ (SF@) 8000 AND 0= SWAP 0< AND FDROP ;

: FDUP0=   ( F: r -- r ; -- flag )
        FSP @ 2+ W@ 8000 AND 0= ;

: F0=   ( F: r -- ; -- flag )
        FDUP0= FDROP ;

: F=    ( F: r1 r2 -- ; -- flag )
        FSP @ 2+ W@ FSP @ 8 + W@ OR 8000 AND 0=    \ both zero
        IF      TRUE
        ELSE    FSP @ (SF@) FSP @ 6 + (SF@) ROT = >R = R> AND
        THEN    F2DROP ;

ALSO HIDDEN DEFINITIONS

: (FCMP)   ( F: r1 r2 -- r1 r2 ; -- -1 | 0 | 1 )   \ compare r1 with r2
        FSP @ 6 + (SF@) S1 ! M1 !  FSP @ (SF@) S2 ! M2 !
        M1 @ 0< 0= M2 @ 0< 0= AND IF  0 EXIT  THEN          \ both zero
        M1 @ 0< 0= IF  S2 @ 8000 AND IF  1 ELSE -1 THEN  EXIT  THEN
        M2 @ 0< 0= IF  S1 @ 8000 AND IF -1 ELSE  1 THEN  EXIT  THEN
        S1 @ S2 @ XOR 8000 AND                          \ signs differ
        IF      S1 @ 8000 AND IF -1 ELSE 1 THEN  EXIT
        THEN
        S1 @ 7FFF AND S2 @ 7FFF AND 2DUP <>             \ magnitudes
        IF      >
        ELSE    2DROP M1 @ M2 @ 2DUP = IF  2DROP 0 EXIT  THEN  U>
        THEN    IF  1  ELSE  -1  THEN
        S1 @ 8000 AND IF  NEGATE  THEN ;

PREVIOUS DEFINITIONS

: F2DUP>   ( F: r1 r2 -- ; -- flag )    \ F-PC native port: leaves r1 r2
        (FCMP) 0> ;

: F2DUP<   ( F: r1 r2 -- ; -- flag )    \ F-PC native port: leaves r1 r2
        (FCMP) 0< ;

PREVIOUS PREVIOUS

: F<    ( F: r1 r2 -- ; -- flag )
        F2DUP< F2DROP ;

: F>    ( F: r1 r2 -- ; -- flag )
        F2DUP> F2DROP ;

: F<=   ( F: r1 r2 -- ; -- flag )
        F2DUP> F2DROP 0= ;

: F>=   ( F: r1 r2 -- ; -- flag )
        F2DUP< F2DROP 0= ;

: FMAX  ( F: r1 r2 -- r3 )
        F2DUP>  IF  FDROP  ELSE  FNIP  THEN ;

: FMIN  ( F: r1 r2 -- r3 )
        F2DUP<  IF  FDROP  ELSE  FNIP  THEN ;

: FABS   ( F: r1 -- r2 )
        FSP @ DUP W@ 7FFF AND SWAP W! ;

: FNEGATE   ( F: r1 -- r2 )
        FSP @ DUP W@ 8000 XOR SWAP W! ;

DECIMAL
